       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. That dose risks serious liver toxicity, and a single 5,000 mg dose is already above the acute toxicity threshold for a 70 kg patient (about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10.5 g). It may be a typo.\n\nTypical adult oral dosing is:\n- **500 to 1,000 mg every 6 to 8 hours**, not to exceed 4 g/day. Many services use a lower ceiling of 3 g/day.\n- **650 mg every 6 hours** or **1,000 mg three times daily**, which are common choices.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. For example, 1,000 mg by mouth three times daily is 3 g/day. Please also confirm the intended dose with your supervising resident or attending."
