       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose, and I can't find a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. It could cause acute liver failure, and nothing you've told me about this patient (70 kg, normal liver and kidney function) makes it safe.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1,000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg every 6 hours. I can enter either right away.\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If they want a different dose, they can clarify the intent or enter the order themselves. If this came from a verbal or written instruction, it may have been a transcription error, such as 500 mg misread as 5,000 mg.\n- **Pharmacy.** A pharmacist can help if there's a specific reason you think a nonstandard dose is needed.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
